{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "U.S. veterans are framed as protectors and community restorers — e.g., David Clark is “busy with projects to destroy unexploded U.S. bombs and help families affected by the Agent Orange defoliant,” and Mark O’Connor provides bicycles to children. Language emphasizes their ongoing work to ensure safety and assist others, fitting a Guardian/virtue role."
  },
