{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Hillary Clinton is framed as a role model and leader in children’s biographies (title cited: “Do All the Good You Can”; theme of female strength). The narrative presents her public-service roles (senator, secretary of state) and the books’ intent to be 'thought-provoking,' which casts her in a virtuous/guardian-like light despite noting flaws."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The text does not portray anyone as a rebel, martyr, or underdog mobilizing change at personal cost; it focuses on biographical depiction and students’ opinions rather than revolutionary sacrifice or outsider struggle."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
