    "explanation": "The federal judge (Mark Goldsmith) and the ACLU lawyers are framed as protectors of legal and moral norms: the judge halted deportations, citing grave harm and giving detainees time to seek counsel, and the ACLU argued to prevent removals that could lead to persecution. Language (e.g., 'Such harm far outweighs any interest the Government may have') positions them as upholding safety and justice."
  },
