    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Boris Johnson is depicted as provoking internal conflict — his 'remarks ... deepened divisions' and he 'set out four personal red lines' that threatened to 'unravel' the union — framing him as an instigator who initiates tension within the party."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "The story contains no depiction of covert plots, espionage, betrayal, systematic deception, or sabotage; tensions are public and political rather than secretive subversion."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "Although the party has been weakened politically ('lost the Conservatives' majority' and 'setback has undermined the party's confidence'), the text does not explicitly frame actors or institutions as corrupt or incompetent in the archetypal sense."
  },
  "Marginalized_Sufferers": {
