{
  "Ethical_Stabilizers": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Theresa May (the home secretary) is framed as a protector/guardian of national order and proper process — calling for ‘rigorous processing’, people to be ‘properly fingerprinted’, returning ‘illegal economic migrants’, and saying Britain will ‘help the most vulnerable people’. Language emphasizes moral authority, law enforcement and stewardship of borders."
  },
