    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "There is no sustained framing of anyone as a rebel, martyr, or underdog sacrificing for systemic change; the piece is partisan critique and calls for reciprocal obstruction, not heroic sacrifice."
  },
  "Overt_Aggressors": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Republicans (and Mitch McConnell) are portrayed as initiators of conflict and obstruction — e.g., framing McConnell’s 2009 vow to “actively work to sabotage the government,” references to “unprecedented obstruction,” and language urging Democrats to “declare war on Trump.” The text also accuses them of racial hostility (“because Republicans hated that a black guy was elected president”), which aligns with the 'Bigot' instantiation of overt aggression."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "Actors are depicted as pretending and hypocritical (e.g., “pretending that they acted like adults,” McConnell “pretending” Republicans treated Obama with deference), and as engaging in sabotage and procedural manipulation (pledging to leave posts unfilled, pressuring to rush confirmations), which frames them as deceivers/saboteurs undermining trust and process."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
