    "explanation": "Protesters are framed as visible antagonists: phrases like \"shutting down our public roads,\" \"hitting these thugs,\" \"illegally blocked traffic,\" and \"creating a traffic nightmare\" cast them as instigators who directly initiate conflict and harm others."
  },
  "Deceptive_Subversives": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The piece explicitly labels a lead protester as a \"George Soros paid operative,\" implying covert manipulation and outside coordination; this language frames at least some protesters as conspiratorial/subversive actors operating through hidden agendas."
  },
  "Institutional_Toxins": {
    "is_used": "Yes",
    "explanation": "The text invokes the GW Bridge episode—\"illegally caused by former aides to Governor Chris Christie\"—as precedent, presenting political aides/institutions as actors who abused power; it also criticizes the media for misattribution, suggesting institutional failure or bias."
