    "explanation": "U.S. officials (Mnuchin/the Treasury) are framed as defenders of established rules and fair practice — e.g., “pushing hard to advance U.S. interests,” pressing to “reaffirm commitments to avoid competitive currency devaluations,” and urging a “fair and open trade” / “level playing field.” This positions them as guardians upholding international norms and economic justice."
  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
